**The headline number is sustained throughput**, not the ingress
rate. While the queue grows, ingress accepts faster than delivery manages
to hand off, and dividing what was accepted by the window length passes a backlog off as
completed work. The sustained figure counts what was delivered over the whole time, including
the {{ (bench_drain_end | int) - (bench_window_end | int) }} s of drain, during which
the queue was drained with no load applied.

The difference between these two numbers shows how far ingress is ahead of
delivery: the larger it is, the more the run leaned on the queue.
